--- body ---
## Context

This ticket was ruled a monster on 2026-09-02 and is now the TRACKER for the
gate estate of SPEC.md §5.2.8. It carried five instruments — fold, golden, RSS,
convergence, soak — across every rung of the ladder at once, with a build-gated
exit and more than one sign-off unit bundled into it. The 2026-08-31 ruling that
partitioned the sheet across five sequential goals had already reordered its
work from instrument order into rung order; the decomposition finishes that
move. Five children, each sized to one sign-off unit, each blocked by its real
prerequisite and never by this tracker.

The ladder is README.md's "## The goals ladder": the number is the build order,
each requirement sits on exactly one rung, and the ruled method is tests first,
bottom-up — a rung is declared only when its assertions run. SPEC.md §5.2.8 owns
every gate and threshold, §5.2.9 every budget; the children cite addresses and
copy no number. Two of the tracker's premises have since gone stale and are
corrected in the children rather than here: the mock Zotero local API does not
"land with" the convergence harness — tranche 1 (ticket 0551, closed) already
built it on the fork branch `conductor-integration` — and the two readings of
R20's letter this body once flagged as awaiting ratification were both ratified
on 2026-08-29, leaving the RSS gate gated instead on §5.2.9's re-pin of three
ceilings after the 2026-09-02 topology.

## Children

- **ticket 0578** — goal 1: the fold sweep, R10's egress clause and R15's
  deletion clause, extending `bench/smoke_upstream.py` against stock upstream at
  the reviewed SHA. Blocked-by: nothing. R22 and R31 stay on goal 1's roster but
  are owned by ticket 0033 and ticket 0488.
- **ticket 0579** — goal 2: R3's counter-churn clause and R23's serving half,
  against a built index on the fork branch `conductor-integration`. Blocked-by:
  nothing open. R13 is ticket 0035's.
- **ticket 0580** — goal 3: the convergence harness and the soak, as the
  executable acceptance spec for R1, R4, R6, R17, R18, R19 at index time and
  R32, over tranche 1's record/replay fixtures. Also the spec served to the
  harness offer, ticket 0032. Blocked-by: ticket 0566.
- **ticket 0581** — the golden gate: SPEC.md §5.2.8's thresholds over the pinned
  set, deciding R34. Blocked-by: ticket 0029.
- **ticket 0582** — the RSS gate: SPEC.md §5.2.9's budgets against the synthetic
  monster, pre-machinery form, server-only and red-with-waiver against the
  document class whose uncapped build measured 2 084,9 MiB. Labelled
  `needs-human`: it needs the ceiling re-pin ratified before it can assert a
  number. Blocked-by: nothing, and blocked all the same. It inherits the subject
  / number split ticket 0550's reconciliation recorded here on 2026-09-02: the
  service clauses have a subject, since ticket 0575 builds the embedding service
  boundary, and two of them still lack a number — the service arm's ceiling is
  ticket 0577's probe, and the worker's kill-at-the-bound assertion needs the
  bound ticket 0554 makes real.

## Invariants

Stated once, here, and inherited by every child:

- **The unit is the MUST clause, not the requirement.** One assertion per
  clause, so `delivered` on README.md becomes a count rather than a reader's
  judgement (absorbed from tracker 0400, dissolved 2026-08-31). R17 is the
  worked example: one MUST, four assertions behind it — N of M, per stage, the
  most-recent-covered date, metadata-only counted with its reason — so the
  clause count is a floor.
- **Honest red and waiver states in the Makefile, never a green that means
  "could not look".** A gate that skips because its machinery is absent reports
  the same thing as one that is broken, and a waiver is a state rather than a
  pass.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] ticket 0578 closed
- [ ] ticket 0579 closed
- [ ] ticket 0580 closed
- [ ] ticket 0581 closed
- [ ] ticket 0582 closed
- [ ] the integration review: with all five closed, re-read the children's
      diffs together, run the full suite, and verify that the gate estate of
      SPEC.md §5.2.8 is one estate rather than five — that `delivered` on
      README.md is a count of assertions that ran, and that no gate reports
      green for a clause nobody asserted
